alse,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\"blind_id\":\"ST068\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States that open-end index and fully transparent active ETFs can rely on the rule and lists UIT ETFs under 'Need separate exemptive relief'.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Lists leveraged/inverse ETFs under the rule, notes the 2020 release removed their exclusion and rescinded their orders, and says they must comply with Rule 18f-4.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":0.5,\"reason\":\"Covers non-transparent/semi-transparent active ETFs and ETF share classes needing separate orders, and the daily holdings disclosure condition. It omits master-feeder structures, so the bundle is incomplete.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"There is no central error. UITs are correctly placed outside the rule, leveraged/inverse ETFs are not categorically excluded, and non-transparent ETFs and share classes are correctly said to need separate relief. The ancillary 18f-4 details (VaR limit, grandfathering, late-2025 staff letters) cannot be refuted from the supplied evidence, so they are not treated as falsehoods. The required-point total is 2.5 of 3 because master-feeder is missing from point 3, so not every required minimum is fully covered. The truncated ending ('My knowledge runs') does not remove any substantive content.\"}\n```","ttft_ms":6756,"type":"result","duration_ms":10652,"uuid":"27af2763-66e8-411c-a3c6-7ee5f6e97cfe","ttft_stream_ms":1235,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":1235,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
